{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "Prithvi API",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "description": "Where the world's things are: SVG maps for Akasha worlds, with articles pinned to them.\n\n**A pin is an article on a map.** Its identity is the article's own address, so one article has at most one place per map, and the world in the path is shared by both -- a pin pointing outside its world cannot be expressed.\n\n**Permissions are Akasha's.** A map's world is an Akasha database, and that database's grants are the map's. There is nothing extra to share. A reader who cannot read a pinned article does not see that pin at all.\n\n**Every change carries `If-Match`.** Absent is `428`, stale is `409`.\n\n**Deleting frees the name.** A delete leaves a tombstone and hides the record; creating the same name again revives it as the next revision, and `restore` is there when you wanted the old contents back rather than a fresh start."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:5002/prithvi",
      "description": "Local docker compose stack"
    },
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:5004",
      "description": "Standalone, in development"
    }
  ],
